--TEST--
a written-out name that is not a public property is a compile error under `as ?property<T>` as well, since the name is decided where it is written — `rule:types/property-key`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Profile {
    public string $city = "Vienna";
    private string $secret = "shut";
}

// The checked form never throws for a written-out name, so the nullable
// form has no throw to replace with `null`: the name is checked here.
?property<Profile> $peek = "secret" as ?property<Profile>;
echo $peek == null ? "null" : "key", "\n";
// covers: lang:types/property-keys
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0405]: `Profile` has no public property `$secret`
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
